  "one_line_summary": "Design rule: replace a pore-surface C-H moiety in MAF-4-like frameworks with an isoelectronic N atom",
  "key_insights": [
    {
      "title": "Mechanism",
      "body": "C-H_moiety_on_framework → uptake"
    },
    {
      "title": "Mechanism",
      "body": "lack_of_strong_adsorption_site_on_pore_surface → uptake"
    },
    {
      "title": "Design Rule",
      "body": "[positive] replace a pore-surface C-H moiety in MAF-4-like frameworks with an isoelectronic N atom → introduces a Lewis base active site for guest binding and enhances sorption performance, especially for more polar adsorbates"
    },
    {
      "title": "Design Rule",
      "body": "[positive] design triazolate-based PCPs so that one triazolate N atom remains uncoordinated after framework construction → preserves pore-surface Lewis base active sites for guest binding"
    },
    {
      "title": "Comparison",
      "body": "MAF-4 and MAF-7 vs these samples: winner=tie on N2_porosity"
    },
    {
      "title": "Comparison",
      "body": "MAF-47-x samples vs MAF-7: winner=subject_a on capillary_evaporation_hysteresis"
    }
  ],
