  "notable_quotes": [
    "MAF-4 is a highly porous and exceptionally stable metal-organic zeolite, but it adsorbs H2, CO2, and C2H2 only weakly because its pore surface lacks strong adsorption sites.",
    "Unlike MAF-7, MAF-47-x shows negligible hysteresis after capillary evaporation; its gating mechanism is pore-surface activity, making it useful for repeated adsorption-desorption cycles.",
    "MAF-4 and MAF-7 show similar high porosity, with pore volumes about 0.67 cm3 g−1 and surface areas about 1870 m2 g−1, exceeding the most open inorganic zeolites."
  ],
